    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d278-a1">

                <pb facs="0453" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg411"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 28, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 22d instant, enclosing a copy of a note addressed by Mr.
                    Seward to Mr. Dayton, the United States minister at Paris.</p>
                <p>As you state that this communication is made solely out of respect to her
                    Majesty’s government and for its information, I have only to say that I accept
                    it in the same spirit, and shall not deem it necessary to enter into any remarks
                    on the despatch to Mr. Dayton, a copy of which is enclosed in your letter.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
